# Madrid-2019 (q = +/- 0.85) + TIP4P/2005.
# One trajectory per row. v and its standard error are the ordinary-least-squares
# slope of the CHILL+ ice thickness (angstrom per nanosecond) and of the
# crystal-oxygen count (molecules per nanosecond). The error is the standard
# error of that slope, not a replicate standard error.
# c_L is the liquid molality in the last frame (mol/kg).
# defects, rings6 and rings5 are means over 51 frames, in the front layer.
# k is the mean rejection coefficient c_ice/c_liquid. It is 0 because no
# ion occupied a bulk-ice bin.
